From 3d6b0132e794257ab8c60930a539e394c3a52006 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pokeheartgold-3ds <bootstrap@invalid>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 03:58:03 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] nnsys: give NNS_G2dInitCellTransferStateManager its return
 type (SDK_PORT_3DS)

lib/include/nnsys/g2d/g2d_CellTransferManager.h:24 declares the function with no
return type, so it is implicitly `int`. MWCC accepts that. GCC 14 and later (devkitARM
16, the toolchain this port builds with) reject implicit int in a declaration as an
error, which stops every NitroSystem and game file that includes the header.

The definition is `int NNS_G2dInitCellTransferStateManager(...)`
(lib/NitroSystem/src/g2d_cell_transfer_manager.c:28), so adding `int` states what
MWCC already assumed. It sits behind #ifdef SDK_PORT_3DS so MWCC compiles the
unchanged header (gcc -E -P without the macro is identical to the unpatched file).

This is a GCC-only fix; it is also a fix the upstream decomp could take as is.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 lib/include/nnsys/g2d/g2d_CellTransferManager.h | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/lib/include/nnsys/g2d/g2d_CellTransferManager.h b/lib/include/nnsys/g2d/g2d_CellTransferManager.h
index 5e2e743..bf96c97 100644
--- a/lib/include/nnsys/g2d/g2d_CellTransferManager.h
+++ b/lib/include/nnsys/g2d/g2d_CellTransferManager.h
@@ -21,6 +21,9 @@ typedef struct NNSG2dCellTransferState {
 
 void NNS_G2dFreeCellTransferStateHandle(u32 handle);
 u32 NNS_G2dGetNewCellTransferStateHandle();
+#ifdef SDK_PORT_3DS
+int
+#endif
 NNS_G2dInitCellTransferStateManager(NNSG2dCellTransferState *pCellStateArray, u32 numCellState, VramTransferTaskRegisterFuncPtr pTaskRegisterFunc);
 void NNS_G2dUpdateCellTransferStateManager(void);
 
